15 0 obj
<< /A 43 0 R /Alt (PRISMA flow diagram detailing study identification, screening, eligibility, and inclusion: 1275 records identified, 517 duplicates removed, 758 screened, 713 excluded for specific reasons, 45 reports sought, 6 not retrieved, 39 assessed, 13 excluded, and 26 studies included in the review.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 44 0 R /Alt (Risk of bias and applicability concerns traffic light plot and corresponding bar chart for included studies across four domains: patient selection, index test, reference standard, and flow and timing. Green indicates low risk or concern, yellow unclear, and red high. Most studies display low risk and concern across domains except for some high and unclear risks in patient selection and index test, as shown in both the matrix and summary bars.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Receiver operating characteristic \(ROC\) curve compares five methods for diagnostic performance, showing sensitivity on the vertical axis and false positive rate on the horizontal axis. Methods include CEUS, CEUS_TIRADS, CEUS_UE, CEUS_AI, and CEUS_US, with area under the curve values ranging from zero point nine one to zero point nine seven.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Network diagrams labeled as panels A and B compare five diagnostic methods: CEUS, CEUS_TIRADS, CEUS_UE, CEUS_AI, and CEUS_US, with node size corresponding to sample size. Thicker lines and numbers indicate more direct comparisons between methods, and panel B features slightly different sample sizes per method compared to panel A.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Receiver operating characteristic \(ROC\) curve graph comparing diagnostic methods, with sensitivity on the y-axis and false positive rate on the x-axis; five colored curves represent CEUS, CEUS_TIRADS, CEUS_UE, CEUS_AI, and CEUS_US, with respective AUC values ranging from 0.92 to 0.97, indicating diagnostic performance.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (Network diagrams labeled A and B compare study connections between five diagnostic methods: CEUS, CEUS_UE, CEUS_TIRADS, CEUS_AI, and CEUS_US. Node size reflects sample size, line thickness corresponds to the number of studies, and numbers on lines indicate study counts.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (Receiver operating characteristic \(ROC\) curve comparison of five methods, each represented by different colored lines and markers, with sensitivity on the y-axis and false positive rate on the x-axis; legend indicates area under curve for each method ranging from zero point eight four to zero point nine eight.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (Network diagrams labeled A and B show five nodes representing diagnostic methods, sized proportionally to participant numbers. Thicker lines indicate more comparisons, with numbers on edges denoting study counts. Nodes labeled CEUS, CEUS_TIRADS, CEUS_US, CEUS_UE, and CEUS_AI are connected by lines, with A displaying larger n values than B.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
